Working-tree stability delta:
- App-info provisioning runs in the package-contained `sls-prelaunch`
  executable before Steam starts. Running it from the rtld-audit callback
  reproduced allocator corruption; the standalone phase completed cleanly.
- PackagePatch, ManifestBind, ReconcilePin, and Parental are enabled as
  optional fail-closed adapters. On Steam build 1784778118 all patterns
  resolved, both libraries mapped, package expansion and parental rewriting
  were exercised, and a two-minute SLS-only launch soak remained stable.
- ReconcilePin redirects only EvaluateConfigChanges' direct target-vector
  builder call. The entry context vector is observation-only because it can
  alias Steam's active/installed state; rewriting it caused a metadata-only
  false success during live Linux downgrade testing.
- Managed DLC quarantine observes two optional, uniquely resolved chunk
  callbacks and filters only the target plan/package-0 injection. It must never
  be broadened to the active/public comparison path.

